meta {
  name: Razorpay Counselling Payment Captured
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/webhooks/counselling/razorpay
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Razorpay-Signature: {{razorpaySignature}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "event": "payment.captured",
    "payload": {
      "payment": {
        "entity": {
          "id": "pay_xxxxxxxxxxxx",
          "order_id": "order_xxxxxxxxxxxx",
          "amount": 50000,
          "currency": "INR",
          "status": "captured",
          "notes": {
            "availability_id": "{{availabilityId}}",
            "student_id": "{{studentId}}"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Razorpay webhook — NOT called manually. Configure this URL in the
  Razorpay Dashboard for the `payment.captured` event.

  ## Signature
  Razorpay signs the raw request body with HMAC-SHA256 using
  RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET, sent as the `X-Razorpay-Signature` header.
  This sample request will fail signature verification unless you
  compute a real signature for the exact raw body bytes — it exists
  here purely to document the contract shape.

  ## Effect
  On a valid `payment.captured` event, the server marks the order as
  paid for (availability_id, student_id) from `payload.payment.entity.notes`,
  for 30 minutes. `POST /api/v1/student/counselling/sessions` (Book Session)
  then consumes this marker to confirm payment without trusting client input.

  Idempotent: duplicate webhook deliveries for the same payment id are
  ignored (Redis key `payment-processed:{paymentId}`, 24h TTL).
}
